    •   Forborne exposures should be reported as overdue when they have been past due for more than 30 days from the original maturity date;
    •   If the exposure is still past due after the end of the grace period, it should be reported as impaired; and
    •   If the exposure is past due but the borrower has provided evidence of its ability to repay the amount within the next 12 months, it should be reported as current.

